
"smart_sources:2026-07-27 - Does Your State Still Steal People’s Homes_.md": {"path":"2026-07-27 - Does Your State Still Steal People’s Homes_.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"dsbmge","at":1785795033967},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785347139541,"size":6624,"at":1785795034036,"hash":"dsbmge"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,21],"###The Pung Case":[22,35],"###The Pung Case#{1}":[24,35],"###What Can You Do?":[36,43],"###What Can You Do?#{1}":[38,43],"###NTUF at ALEC":[44,50],"###NTUF at ALEC#{1}":[46,50]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Andrew Wilford","target":"Andrew Wilford","line":5},{"title":"argument","target":"https://www.ntu.org/foundation/detail/ntuf-argues-that-minnesotas-draconian-property-tax-laws-are-excessive-fines-and-violate-the-constitution","line":18},{"title":"declared","target":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/25-95_dc8e.pdf","line":28},{"title":"tried to tell","target":"https://www.ntu.org/library/doclib/2025/12/Pung-v-Isabella-County-Amicus.pdf","line":38}],"metadata":{"title":"Does Your State Still Steal People’s Homes?","source":"https://www.ntu.org/foundation/detail/does-your-state-still-steal-peoples-homes","author":["[[Andrew Wilford]]"],"published":"2026-07-27","created":"2026-07-29","description":"Last month, the Supreme Court handed down its ruling in Pung v. Isabella County. In doing so, it failed to administer the coup de grace to the practice of home equity theft in the few states that still allow some form of it.   The good news: lawmakers in those states can and should solve this problem themselves.  Home equity theft occurs when local governments seize properties to cover unpaid property tax debts, but then keep the entire proceeds of the sale, even when it exceeds the tax debt, pe, Author(s): Andrew Wilford"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},